    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d334">

                <pb facs="0420" n="316" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg316"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4227</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Far Eastern
                        Affairs (Hornbeck)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-13">February 13, 1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have spoken to the British Ambassador and have informed him of the information
                    contained in Shanghai’s 43, February 13, 1 p.m.; also that we think that the
                    position taken by the American Consul General at Shanghai is the correct one and
                    that we are telegraphing the Consul General approving the position taken by
                    him.</p>
                <p>The British Ambassador stated that he had received subsequent to <pb facs="0421"
                        n="317" xml:id="pg317"/> our conversation of February 3 (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">4?</hi>) no further information on the matter.</p>
                <p>I stated that it was obvious that the decision reached by the British Consul
                    General and that reached by the American Consul General were opposites; that we
                    regretted this, as we had instructed our Consul General to confer with the
                    British Consul General and try to arrange for the same course to be taken by
                    both.</p>
                <p>The Ambassador said that he also regretted it, but it looked as though the
                    American Consul General’s decision were sound. He thanked me for informing him
                    and said he would inform his Government.</p>
                <closer><signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">tanley</hi>] K. H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ornbeck</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
